{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ומלק את ראשו", :translit "u-malaq et rosho", :gloss "and he shall wring off its head"} {:he "מליקה מן הצואר", :translit "meliqah min ha-tzavar", :gloss "meliqa (wringing) from the neck"} {:he "כשהיא פודחת מחזרת הסימנים ע\"ג הצואר", :translit "k'she-hi podachat machazeret ha-simanim al-gav ha-tzavar", :gloss "when it is being strangled it returns the signs atop the neck"} {:he "ועולת העוף למעלה", :translit "ve-olat ha-of le-ma'lah", :gloss "and the burnt offering of the fowl is above"} {:he "יונת אלם", :translit "yonat eilem", :gloss "dove of silence"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Dove (yonah) homonym links the bird-offering to Isaac called yonat eilem"}], :frame {:text "The procedure of meliqa for bird offerings is defined as cutting or pinching at the back of the neck rather than full slaughter, taught in Chullin 20a-b. Isaac is called יונת אלם (dove of silence) because his name (where the letter ח is silent) is written in Genesis 22:2.", :sources ["Chullin 20a-b" "Genesis 22:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Dove (yonah) homonym links the bird-offering to Isaac called yonat eilem", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:01.131629679Z", :model "glm-5.2"}